            <infoLink name="MT|RG Masters Of Obfuscation (Minor)" id="653b-87bb-f533-84b8" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="5913-86c8-ea33-43da"/>
            <infoLink name="MT|RG Shadowkin (Flaw)" id="9957-99a4-9864-1587" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="fe87-b409-e7ed-210d"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="a5b1-4d65-2ca3-2242"/>
          </constraints>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XX: Alpha Legion (SL)" hidden="false" id="98a6-7b7c-52e9-6fb9" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" sortIndex="18" page="148">
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="MT|AL Look After Their Own (Flaw)" id="567c-bc0c-2a01-3bc4" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="cd97-0c67-3e00-080c"/>
            <infoLink name="MT|AL Masters Of Misdirection (Minor)" id="ed5b-39c7-18c1-28fe" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="3805-9693-2e77-2cdc"/>
            <infoLink name="MT|AL Assassination Tactics (Major)" id="076d-3937-d8f2-6edb" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="8bd7-1028-8a58-a828"/>
            <infoLink name="MT|AL Master of Subterfuge (Hero)" id="7a2c-dbba-1bf1-3eaf" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="3405-3e8f-0ea7-1277"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="cbfb-8b82-51cd-69aa"/>
          </constraints>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="2" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6e2f-3966-81a2-d5c5"/>
        <constraint type="max" value="3" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3399-4f27-1ff3-ebb4"/>
      </constraints>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Mutable Tactics Traits (Major)" id="4c42-2619-2e5a-659c" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="I: Dark Angels (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="2611-606a-d359-1b70" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140" sortIndex="1">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|DA Ruthless Bladesmen (Major)" id="6ad2-cfd9-fc21-3bb6" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>If this unit is the winner in an Assault, each enemy unit that lost suffers an additional -1 penalty to the resulting Morale check.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2f9b-630e-b120-7f09"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="80d1-09cd-7916-3524" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="III: Emperor&apos;s Children (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="6459-8ea8-08d4-b7d2" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140" sortIndex="2">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|EC Unparalleled Skill (Major)" id="cc0f-ca91-37c7-6c3e" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>When making a To Hit roll in the Assault phase for a model in this unit, a result of 4+ is always successful.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2737-b058-191c-af5f"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="09f0-afd4-aed5-dfcc" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="IV: Iron Warriors (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="2db0-1fff-f251-862d" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141" sortIndex="3">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IW Ruthless Precision (Major)" id="9fad-cf42-cdb1-469b" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>When making a Shooting Attack, this unit gains a bonus of +1 to all Armour Penetration rolls, and a bonus of +1 to To Wound rolls made against units with the Automata or Dreadnought Unit Types.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9b51-02b0-e824-a41f"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="354d-b21e-1c88-f53a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="V: White Scars (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="4af0-98db-27b6-6bc4" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141" sortIndex="4">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WS Swift Of Action (Major)" id="eb7a-cd23-4dc5-5e50" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>Each time this unit runs, it gains the Shrouded (5+) special rule until the start of the Active player’s next turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e40e-c1d1-c43f-80ac"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="fcf9-3de6-e2e7-04e6" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VI: Space Wolves (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="034a-f25d-55a0-4aea" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142" sortIndex="5">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SW Spirit Of Fenris (Major)" id="aba0-3282-7198-1d13" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit successfully Charges, all models in this unit gain a bonus of +1 To Wound.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3ef7-6a70-39d7-2a20"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="59b5-8b5d-0fb6-97c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VII: Imperial Fists (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="b1e1-ecc2-5e7d-d6c2" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142" sortIndex="6">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IF Devastating Volleys (Major)" id="ee4d-3d15-8235-f0ef" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>The unit gains a bonus of +1 to all To Wound rolls with bolt pistols, combi-bolters and bolters as part of any Shooting Attack (including as part of any Reaction).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c32f-a1e0-91c0-40b9"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4412-9c1b-b870-3e0b" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VIII: Night Lords (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="c221-efc6-d394-e350" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143" sortIndex="7">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|NL Murderous Intent (Major)" id="3f3d-bc9c-a706-f664" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>At the start of the Fight sub-phase, if this unit outnumbers the enemy models in that combat, models in this unit gain a bonus of +1 to To Hit rolls until the end of the Phase. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as a number of models equal to the value included as part of that special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2010-de51-dfd3-a709"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4122-11fc-c202-14c3" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="IX: Blood Angels (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="26aa-b8f8-9497-e7d1" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143" sortIndex="8">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|BA Vengeful Blow (Major)" id="d1c9-055a-9dc1-224e" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit successfully Charges, or is successfully Charged, all models in this unit gain a bonus of +1 To Wound when making attacks with weapons that do not have the Unwieldy special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="ed85-4712-aa3c-e3b4"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="d259-8392-ebda-3e52" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="X: Iron Hands (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="c9b0-88b6-1ade-70a2" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144" sortIndex="9">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IH Unleash The Storm (Major)" id="6fc5-5c8b-0841-9ca0" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>Each time a model in this unit makes a Shooting Attack that targets a unit within 12&quot;, it gains a bonus of +1 to all To Wound rolls made during that Shooting Attack.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="03d6-2fab-daaf-5931"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ae9d-6362-6a6b-3b3a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XII: World Eaters (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="1b39-8677-de2f-8520" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144" sortIndex="10">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WE Violent Intent (Major)" id="96de-3a6f-9bd0-fd29" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>When making a Charge roll for this unit, roll one additional D6 and discard one of the results.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9073-ae15-5266-aa05"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="31b1-96a6-b50a-0305" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIII: Ultramarines (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="fb8c-3021-e7c5-f3a5" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145" sortIndex="11">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|UM Methodical Fighters (Major)" id="32ec-a5bd-91a5-c5aa" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>Each time this unit makes a Shooting Attack or declares a Charge, if an enemy unit declares a Reaction, its controlling player must make a Leadership test for that unit before expending a point from their Reaction Allotment. If that test is failed, that unit cannot make a Reaction during this Phase.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="091e-e6f8-c5b0-e28c"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3697-65e5-2eee-495c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIV: Death Guard (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="75d7-1918-8dfc-a526" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145" sortIndex="12">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|DG Inexorable Assault (Major)" id="5f32-7a60-9ed3-d524" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>If every model in this unit has not moved more than 7&quot; in the controlling player’s Movement phase, it is counted as Stationary when making Shooting Attacks until the start of the controlling player’s next turn. This does not apply to units with the Vehicle Unit Type or Artillery Unit Sub-type.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1b76-1e5f-4422-e6ba"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7269-248a-cd22-03fa" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XV: Thousand Sons (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="0df7-81bd-808a-9f56" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146" sortIndex="13">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|TS Wielders Of The Warp (Major)" id="b224-c37c-33eb-c8ea" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>One non-Vehicle Thousand Sons model in this unit gains the Prosperine Wrath Psychic Weapon, and is treated as having the Psyker Unit Sub-type for the purposes of using it (note that this does not give that model access to any other Psychic Disciplines).
*The Strength Characteristic of this Psychic Weapon is equal to 3 plus the number of Thousand Sons models in this unit, to a maximum of Strength 10.
(BS Note: Psyker Unit type not added on BS as it only applies to 1 model each phase, and only if they are the major component of the unit.)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="51da-6adc-c903-2301"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Prosperine Wrath" typeId="cede-0217-1b10-2a34" typeName="Psychic Weapon" hidden="false" id="1082-6f0f-2f8c-f9e5">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="62ec-fbf5-5252-0d17">24&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="17ff-12e7-77d3-2fbe">*</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="f431-a7b9-d9d0-36c9">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="2159-62b6-4337-d516">Assault 1, Rending (6+), Psychic Focus</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Psychic Focus" id="daa5-be45-74b8-4178" hidden="false" type="rule" targetId="bff3-3548-b2b8-72f1"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ec51-bdcd-862c-3899" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVI: Sons of Horus (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="173f-9084-c487-eeb8" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146" sortIndex="14">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SoH Punishing Volley (Major)" id="ddbb-5a7b-517d-873f" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>Each time a model in this unit makes a Shooting Attack that targets a unit within 12&quot;, it gains a bonus of +1 to all To Hit rolls made during that Shooting Attack</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="d9d5-e723-b00b-ff0c"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f83b-93b6-9494-e9c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVII: Word Bearers (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="b2c5-1e9a-5955-ab39" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147" sortIndex="15">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WB Zealous Devotion (Major)" id="5511-0371-868b-946f" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit has successfully Charged, if it is part of a combat that results in a draw, then a side that includes this unit is counted as having won the combat by 1 point. If both sides include models with this special rule then the combat remains a draw.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e074-4bd5-c41c-bc43"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3128-d6dd-15e3-586d" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVIII: Salamanders (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="61e0-0593-e4ff-122a" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147" sortIndex="16">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SAL Scions Of The Flame (Major)" id="27b4-aa61-fb1e-553f" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>When a model in this unit makes a Shooting Attack, attacks made with weapons with the Flame, Melta, Plasma or Volkite types gain a bonus of +1 To Wound.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="075f-2427-60e6-0e6c"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="0516-835b-a0d4-e87c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIX: Raven Guard (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="efc0-bfc4-1544-9ed4" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148" sortIndex="17">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|RG Expert Snipers (Major)" id="e6d7-e2a2-8016-d49f" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>Each time this unit makes a Shooting Attack (excluding attacks made with Heavy or Ordnance weapons), the controlling player can allocate the first Wound.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6bcb-6d82-4157-8f52"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5cb4-3c55-d967-cf27" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XX: Alpha Legion (MT | Major)" hidden="true" id="f2fa-68cd-0c59-2cee" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148" sortIndex="18">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|AL Assassination Tactics (Major)" id="8bd7-1028-8a58-a828" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit has successfully Charged, Alpha Legion models in this unit have the Precision Strikes (5+) special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1b0e-8357-5173-561b"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="98a6-7b7c-52e9-6fb9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="b847-db29-f569-26db"/>
        <constraint type="max" value="3" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="263d-8e8c-7632-1cd8"/>
      </constraints>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Mutable Tactics Traits (Minor/Flaw)" id="319a-43d5-28c0-6d4e" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="I: Dark Angels (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="f23f-7549-d4a7-eaa1" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140" sortIndex="1">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|DA Children Of Old Night (Minor)" id="67cc-420b-b06f-1d21" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>This unit makes all Snap Shots at BS 2 instead of BS 1.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|DA Bound By The Hekonystika (Flaw)" id="8adc-b287-3288-08d2" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>Reduce the Leadership Characteristic of all models in this unit by -1.
(BS Note: Stats not changed on BS)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e69b-738c-28d1-1f0a"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="80d1-09cd-7916-3524" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="III: Emperor&apos;s Children (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="14a1-6b82-5950-0431" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140" sortIndex="2">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|EC Expert Duellists (Minor)" id="7ca7-45d9-0052-5e6a" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>Emperor’s Children models in this unit gain the Chosen Warriors special rule.
(BS Note: Stats not changed on BS)</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|EC Warrior&apos;s Pride (Flaw)" id="892f-9fa9-05e9-71d0" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="140">
              <description>If you choose to refuse a Challenge and there was an eligible Emperor’s Children model from this unit that could have accepted, models in this unit suffer a -1 penalty to all To Hit rolls until the end of that turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3f58-f2aa-0592-9911"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="09f0-afd4-aed5-dfcc" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="IV: Iron Warriors (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="7bd8-caf0-a666-9ec7" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141" sortIndex="3">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IW Accustomed To Devastation (Minor)" id="a1b0-63a9-738c-677c" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>Models in this unit are considered to have a Leadership Characteristic of 10 when resolving Morale checks in the Shooting phase.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|IW Uncontrolled Volleys (Flaw)" id="c539-41a3-2791-bb32" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>When making a Shooting Attack as part of a Reaction, weapons used for that Shooting Attack by Iron Warriors models in this unit have the Gets Hot special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="d0e5-c1bf-fddb-c6c6"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="354d-b21e-1c88-f53a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="V: White Scars (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="8160-4e10-1086-6ace" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141" sortIndex="4">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WS Fleet-Footed (Minor)" id="d787-6f8a-c0b8-3960" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>When Running, making Sweeping Advances or moving as part of a Reaction, all models in this unit count their Initiative as 6.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|WS Restless Temperament (Flaw)" id="f99c-0fb4-5a61-a761" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="141">
              <description>If every model in this unit does not end the Movement phase at least 4&quot; from where it began that Phase, each model in that unit suffers a -1 penalty to its Leadership Characteristic until the start of the Active player’s next turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="fbc2-3335-d462-7ec2"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="fcf9-3de6-e2e7-04e6" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VI: Space Wolves (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="2044-e799-3a0f-a59a" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142" sortIndex="5">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SW One Hand On Their Blade (Minor)" id="c7a1-bdf0-3780-309a" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>Models in this unit can still fire bolters or bolt pistols in a turn in which they have Run. If they do so, they must fire Snap Shots.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|SW Undisciplined Assault (Flaw)" id="9427-ee37-d9f0-5647" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>Each time this unit is selected to make a Charge, the controlling player must make a Leadership test for it. If that test is failed, that Charge is Disordered.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="ce4b-4d62-58b9-0b66"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="59b5-8b5d-0fb6-97c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VII: Imperial Fists (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="c982-169b-7ea2-c217" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142" sortIndex="6">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IF Defensive Instincts (Minor)" id="52c6-5262-e5d1-3381" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>Improve the cover save models in this unit have by 1 (e.g., a model in this unit who has a 5+ Cover Save instead has a 4+ Cover Save). This does not grant a Cover Save to a model that is not eligible for one.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|IF Surety Of Action (Flaw)" id="50ab-0fd7-5f00-6876" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="142">
              <description>If the controlling player has any of their Reaction Allotment remaining, this unit must make a Reaction if eligible to do so.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="685d-9e6c-c218-2187"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4412-9c1b-b870-3e0b" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="VIII: Night Lords (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="8a17-6b6b-4f2d-7439" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143" sortIndex="7">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|NL Trophy Takers (Minor)" id="60fd-0ae8-3077-986d" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>When making a Sweeping Advance with this unit, you can roll an additional D6 and discard one of them.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|NL Wary Of A Fair Fight (Flaw)" id="81ba-8aae-c95f-a998" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>This unit may not declare a Charge unless it outnumbers the target unit. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as a number of models equal to the value included as part of that special rule. In addition, if this unit is the closer in an Assault, it suffers an additional -1 penalty to the resulting Morale check.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="39ef-46c3-9533-5cd6"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="4122-11fc-c202-14c3" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="IX: Blood Angels (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="a4c8-4d0a-abab-0709" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143" sortIndex="8">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|BA Encarmine Guile (Minor)" id="9c53-21ab-e630-d697" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit successfully Charged, Blood Angels models in this unit gain the Hammer of Wrath (1) special rule.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|BA Furious Bloodlust (Flaw)" id="7b34-f6c7-261e-d260" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="143">
              <description>This unit must declare a Charge in any of the controlling player’s Assault phases if it is eligible to do so and there is at least one model from any enemy unit within 12&quot; and line of sight of it.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="82e0-60f5-917e-7d47"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="d259-8392-ebda-3e52" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="X: Iron Hands (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="2f1f-a953-2f24-0998" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144" sortIndex="9">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|IH Iron Resolve (Minor)" id="f8a5-20c5-acd7-601a" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>Each time a Shooting Attack is allocated to an Iron Hands model in this unit, that model gains the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule against that attack.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|IH Overly Cautous (Flaw)" id="4c94-cbc9-79a7-2ab5" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>This unit may not Run or make Sweeping Advances</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1649-b913-e74a-ad17"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ae9d-6362-6a6b-3b3a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XII: World Eaters (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="e218-edc9-d8c9-dbff" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144" sortIndex="10">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WE Raging Slayers (Minor)" id="9735-2b30-3683-ba7b" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit successfully Charges, the first failed Armour Saving throw for this unit in that Fight sub-phase is ignored (this has no effect if the weapon’s Armour Piercing value is equal to or lower than the model’s Armour Save).</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|WE Berserker Frustration (Flaw)" id="57c2-d0c9-1e94-f452" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="144">
              <description>If this unit is within 12&quot; of an enemy unit and a Charge is not declared for it during the controlling player’s Assault phase, the controlling player must make a Pinning test for this unit.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8ae0-884f-0cad-f0f3"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="31b1-96a6-b50a-0305" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIII: Ultramarines (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="f153-c2b4-59d3-e118" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145" sortIndex="11">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|UM Prepared Attack (Minor)" id="040a-1869-b523-dabb" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>Each time this unit makes a Shooting Attack as part of a Reaction, add +1 to To Hit rolls for that Shooting Attack.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|UM Strict Chain Of Command (Flaw)" id="839b-c3bb-7da5-44aa" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>Each time this unit is selected to make a Reaction, make a Leadership test for this unit before expending a point from your Reaction Allotment. If this Test is failed, that unit cannot make a Reaction during this Phase.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="84bf-37f6-ea47-aaf4"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3697-65e5-2eee-495c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIV: Death Guard (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="9fbb-e5ec-4857-2a9d" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145" sortIndex="12">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|DG Children Of Barbarus (Minor)" id="987b-0ad3-d2b9-e4dc" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>Non-Vehicle models in this unit gain a 3+ Invulnerable Save against Wounds suffered as a result of Dangerous Terrain tests.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|DG Unhurried Death (Flaw)" id="e088-c140-173e-fb25" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="145">
              <description>When this unit Runs, makes a Sweeping Advance or moves as part of a Reaction, models in this unit are treated as having an Initiative Characteristic of 2.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9153-0a70-fff6-3091"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7269-248a-cd22-03fa" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XV: Thousand Sons (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="693e-669f-1496-429b" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146" sortIndex="13">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|TS Conjured Illusions (Minor)" id="4566-2051-ae79-9d3a" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>If this unit Falls Back from combat, models in this unit are treated as having an Initiative Characteristic of 6 for the purposes of Sweeping Advances.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|TS Undisciplined Mystics (Flaw)" id="027e-d662-96ef-5b2b" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>Whenever a result of 11 or 12 is rolled for a Morale check or Pinning test for this unit, this unit suffers Perils of the Warp.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="a389-a825-24f9-bb68"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="ec51-bdcd-862c-3899" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVI: Sons of Horus (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="fe36-6bda-fb4c-d693" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146" sortIndex="14">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SoH Legacy Of Brutality (Minor)" id="d06f-6e45-cbd9-61c0" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>At the start of the Fight sub-phase, if this unit is outnumbered by enemy models in that combat, models in this unit gain a bonus of +1 to To Hit rolls until the end of the phase. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as a number of models equal to the value included as part of that special rule.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|SoH Towering Arrogance (Flaw)" id="7a33-4d44-f9c0-7d01" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="146">
              <description>Each time this unit is eligible to declare a Reaction to a Shooting Attack or Charge declared by an enemy unit if this unit outnumbers that enemy unit, this unit is not eligible to make a Reaction. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as a number of models equal to the value included as part of that special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e717-d0de-a06b-7e39"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f83b-93b6-9494-e9c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVII: Word Bearers (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="06a7-4d59-98f3-9fbb" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147" sortIndex="15">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|WB Righteous Determination (Minor)" id="d52c-7a62-2b9f-d4ff" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>When making a Morale check or Pinning test for this unit, roll one additional D6 and discard one before determining the result.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|WB Eternal Penitents (Flaw)" id="fc8d-7e67-8abb-d717" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>When this unit fails a Leadership test, Morale check or Pinning test, it suffers one automatic Wound with no saves or Damage Mitigation rolls of any kind allowed.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="f8ba-239f-e303-8b5a"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="3128-d6dd-15e3-586d" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XVIII: Salamanders (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="3063-a59a-ed33-02b8" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147" sortIndex="16">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|SAL Steadfast Bulwark (Minor)" id="2636-f334-c602-ed42" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>During a turn in which this unit is successfully Charged, all models in this unit gain the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule until the end of the turn.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|SAL Prudent Fighters (Flaw)" id="69f2-175f-c745-8f31" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="147">
              <description>This unit may not declare Shooting Attacks or Charges that target units that are Falling Back and may not make Sweeping Advances.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="d407-f674-0e55-7683"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="0516-835b-a0d4-e87c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XIX: Raven Guard (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="dfea-1145-fc23-2889" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148" sortIndex="17">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|RG Masters Of Obfuscation (Minor)" id="5913-86c8-ea33-43da" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>Each time an enemy unit makes a Shooting Attack that targets this unit, if the closest model in this unit is more than 18&quot; away, all models in this unit have the Shrouded (6+) special rule against that Shooting Attack.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|RG Shadowkin (Flaw)" id="fe87-b409-e7ed-210d" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>Each time this unit makes a Morale check, if it is not wholly within a zone of Area Terrain, subtract -1 from the Leadership Characteristic of models in this unit.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="c551-c707-9df2-f714"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5cb4-3c55-d967-cf27" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="XX: Alpha Legion (MT | Minor/Flaw)" hidden="true" id="4428-5e7a-caec-9108" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148" sortIndex="18">
          <rules>
            <rule name="MT|AL Masters Of Misdirection (Minor)" id="3805-9693-2e77-2cdc" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>If an enemy unit makes a Shooting Attack that targets this unit, and there is another eligible target unit that is closer to the enemy unit making the Shooting Attack, models in this unit gain the Shrouded (6+) special rule for the duration of that Shooting Attack.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="MT|AL Look After Their Own (Flaw)" id="cd97-0c67-3e00-080c" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="148">
              <description>When allocating Wounds to models in this unit, the controlling player must allocate Wounds to a non-Alpha Legion model if possible.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="83cb-b70d-ffde-8c9f"/>
          </constraints>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="98a6-7b7c-52e9-6fb9" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="d322-c689-6a55-a08a"/>
        <constraint type="max" value="3" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="9d9d-e42a-4395-9990"/>
      </constraints>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="21e5-9f49-deea-a974" name="Malfunction" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="229 &amp; 253" hidden="false">
      <description>If a weapon with this special rule is used to make a Shooting Attack as part of any Reaction, it gains the Gets Hot special rule for that Shooting Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8f98-3f81-35dc-8a23" name="Stormwing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type gain a bonus of +1 To Hit when rolling To Hit as part of a Shooting Attack (including during a Reaction) with a bolter, combibolter or bolt pistol.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5e82-8a8f-d64f-0839" name="Deathwing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type gain a bonus of +1 To Hit when rolling To Hit in an assault with one of the following weapons: chainsword, force sword, power sword, Terranic greatsword, Calibanite warblade, Charnabal sabre, and Paragon blades or close combat weapons modelled as swords. In addition, a model with the Vehicle Unit Type gains a +1 bonus to the Strength of all Hits inflicted as part of a Ram Attack (up to a maximum of Strength 10).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bbfb-b03e-a6c8-ecae" name="Dreadwing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type reduce the Strength of all attacks made against them with Flame, Plasma, Volkite and Phosphex weapons by -1, and force all attacks made against them with the Poisoned (X) special rule to increase the roll needed to Wound by 1 (to a maximum of 6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3596-4350-5053-a738" name="Ironwing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type may re-roll failed To Hit rolls of ‘1’ when targeting an enemy model with the Vehicle Unit Type. Additionally, a model with this Unit Sub-type and the Vehicle Unit Type makes all Snap Shots at BS 2 instead of BS 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1e3b-0c10-9bb0-8e44" name="Firewing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type gain a bonus of +1 To Wound when attacking a unit that contains at least one model with the Independent Character special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cebe-61d8-8299-0ac9" name="Ravenwing" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="151" hidden="false">
      <description>All models in a unit under the effect of this Hexagrammaton Unit Sub-type, other than models with the Vehicle Unit Type, add +1 to the distance moved when the unit Runs, and models with the Cavalry Unit Type may also re-roll any failed Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls. Models with this Unit Sub-type and the Vehicle Unit Type instead add +2 to their Movement Characteristic when moving at Cruising Speed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="655c-988f-74b5-7e17" name="Dragon&apos;s Breath" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="312" hidden="false">
      <description>When attacking using the Wall of Death special rule, a weapon with this special rule Inflicts D6 Hits instead of D3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="29d7-fe2c-24ee-07f9" name="The Prosperine Arcana" publicationId="09c5-eeae-f398-b653" page="255" hidden="false">
      <description>All models with the Character and Psyker Unit Sub-types in a Thousand Sons Detachment must select one Minor Arcana upgrade from the following options during army selection, before the beginning of the battle.

If a unit includes more than one model with the Character Unit Sub-type then all those models must select the same upgrade from this special rule. No model may have or use more than one option from this special rule, unless another special rule specifically states that they can: (BS NOTE: use named power selected- Athanaen, Cordivae, Pavoni, Pyrae or Raptora)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c56f-80ff-5d8e-1af4" name="Achean Force" publicationId="09c5-eeae-f398-b653" page="259" hidden="false">
      <comment>validated nsh 2022/06/20</comment>
      <description>The controlling player of any unit that includes one or more models with the Psyker Unit Sub-type and a weapon or ability with this special rule, may choose to activate this special rule before making any attacks with that weapon or resolving the ability. To activate this special rule, the controlling player must make a single Psychic check using the Leadership Characteristic of any model in the unit that does not have the Independent Character special rule (unless the unit is entirely composed of models with the Independent Character special rule, in which case the controlling player can select which of those model’s Leadership Characteristics is used). If the Check is successful, then the Strength value of all attacks made with weapons or abilities with this special rule is increased by +2 (In addition to any Modifiers the attack or weapon may already possess), this benefit is applied only in the Phase in which these attack are made and ends immediately after that phase is resolved. If the check is failed then no benefit is gained, but the models in that unit may attack as normal.

All &apos;Achean Force&apos; weapons are counted as &apos;Force&quot; weapons for those rules that affect such weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="edb9-295b-5d36-8fd7" name="Apothecarion Detachment (LA)" publicationId="a716-c1c4-7b26-8424" page="116" hidden="false">
      <description>An Apothecarion Detachment is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed to the battlefield, all models in an Apothecarion Detachment must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment of the army they were selected as part of. Legion Apothecaries that have not selected a Legion Spatha combat bike or Legion Scimitar jetbike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type and the same Legiones Astartes (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary, and may not join units that have Terminator armour of any kind. Legion Apothecaries that have selected a Legion Spatha combat bike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with Legion Spatha combat bikes and the same Legiones Astartes (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary, and any Legion Apothecaries that have selected a Legion Scimitar jetbike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with Legion Scimitar jetbikes and the same Legiones Astartes (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary. No Apothecary may be assigned to any unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes an Apothecary as normal during either deployment or any following turn). No more than one Apothecary may be assigned to any given unit.

Once assigned to a unit, the Legion Apothecary is considered part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances – if that unit is removed as a casualty when the Legion Apothecary is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points are ever scored for removing an Legion Apothecary as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Legion Apothecary gains all of the special rules (with the exception of those that specifically forbid it, such as the Bitter Duty special rule) and Unit Sub-types listed for the unit to which it is attached, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to the unit to which it is assigned.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5529-bb7a-9448-b1f5" name="Hexagrammatic Wards" publicationId="d0df-7166-5cd3-89fd" page="12" hidden="false">
      <description>Any roll To Wound for an attack made with a Psychic Weapon against a model with this special rule suffers a penalty of -1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a2ef-63a4-3531-db91" name="Legiones Cybernetica" publicationId="a716-c1c4-7b26-8424" page="115" hidden="false">
      <description>An army that includes a model with this special rule may take a single Castellax Battle-automata Maniple or a single Vorax Battle-automata Maniple as part of the same Force Organisation choice as the model with this special rule. Any models in the Castellax Battle-automata Maniple or Vorax Battle-automata Maniple included in an army due to this special rule gain the same Legiones Astartes (X) special as the Legion Praevian they share a Force Organization choice with, but may not select any Legion specific Wargear or other options.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2f3e-89a5-27e0-33b7" name="Death-sworn Companions" publicationId="817a-6288-e016-7469" page="165" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit that includes at least one model with this special rule ignores the effects of the Precision Strikes (X), Precision Shots (X), and Sniper special rules, and casualties from Shooting and Melee Attacks are always allocated to a model of the controlling player&apos;s choice.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="752f-1b0d-5888-22b5" name="Skill Unmatched" publicationId="09c5-eeae-f398-b653" page="155" hidden="false">
      <description>When a combat that involves one or more models with this special rule is resolved, before the start of initiative step 10 the controlling player of any models in that combat with this special rule may select on of three following options and apply the effects of that option to all models with this special rule for the duration of that Assault phase. When a unit contains more than one unit with this special rule, then all models in that unit must select the same option if one is chose:

A Perfect Guard: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this option, they must increase their Weapon Skill by +1 for the purposes of determining the score required for enemy models to make To Hit rolls only, but must reduce their Attacks Characteristic by -1.

A Perfect Strike: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this option, they must increase their Weapon Skill by +1 for the purpose of determining the score required for that model&apos;s To Hit rolls targeting enemy models only, but must reduce their Attacks Characteristic by -1.

A Perfect Fury: If a model or models with the Skill Unmatched special rule selects this option, they must increase their Attacks by +1, but must reduce their Weapon Skill by -1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5615-04df-fb39-aa5d" name="Living Icons" publicationId="09c5-eeae-f398-b653" page="155" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with this special rule, and all models in any friendly unit with the Legiones Astartes (Emperor&apos;s Children) special rule and at least one model withing 6&quot; of a model with this special rule, gains +1 to the score used to calculate the winner of a combat during the Assault phase. The effects of this special rule do not stack, and any given unit can only be affected by a single instance of this special rule - however, the effects of this special rule do stack with the effects of Fulgrim&apos;s Sire of the Emperor&apos;s Children special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="be8a-5395-7470-d45b" name="Cloaked in Murder" publicationId="7f9d-5e88-241d-e861" page="13" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit composed entirely of models with this special rule declares a Charge targeting a unit that is already engaged in combat, the Charge roll gains an additional +1 modifier, and if the  Charge is successful then all models in the Charging unit gain +1 To Hit for the duration of the turn in which that Charge is made.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7cdc-4095-eb1e-2b07" name="Sacred Trust" hidden="false">
      <description>Any models with the Infantry or Cavalry Unit Type in the same unit as a model with this special rule may re-roll any failed It Will Not Die rolls made. This effect immediately ends if the model with the Sacred Trust special rule is removed as a casualty or otherwise leaves the unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1864-f270-d462-ecb5" name="Ravening Madmen" hidden="false">
      <description>Any model making a To Wound roll in the Assault phase against a unit composed entirely of models with this special rule reduces its Strength by -1 when determining the score required To Wound (this does not affect the attacking unit&apos;s Strength for the purposes of inflicting Instant Death). Additionally, any To Hit rolls made in the Assault phase targeting a unit that includes one or more models with this special rule, always count the majority Weapon Skill of the target unit as 3, regardless of the actual Weapon Skill of the models in that unit.

A unit that includes models with this special rule may only be joined by models with this special rule, or the Primarch Angron, and models with this special rule may not join a unit that includes any models without this special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ffcb-13b4-9b4c-84da" name="Legiones Astartes (X)" publicationId="e77a-823a-da94-16b9" page="242" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit with this special rule will have a number of additional special rules and abilities specific to their ‘named’ Legion, all of which will be defined in other Horus Heresy – Age of Darkness publications. A Space Marine unit may only have one such ‘named’ rule, e.g., Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus). Space Marine units from a different Legion may only be included in an army using an Allied Detachment (see page 281) and in conjunction with the Allies in the Age of Darkness chart found on page 282.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6659-e858-cfbf-3ff9" name="Ignore Crew Shaken and Stunned (Hammer of Olympia)" hidden="false">
      <description>All Legion Predator Squadrons, Legion Vindicator Squadrons, Land Raider Proteus Carriers and Legion Land Raider Spartan models in a Detachment using this Rite of War ignore the effects of the Crew Shaken and Crew Stunned results on the Vehicle Damage table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7ca5-9127-867f-0a57" name="Shrapnel Weapons Reroll 1s to Hit (Hammer of Olympia)" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit composed entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Iron Warriors) special rule that is part of a Detachment using this Rite of War may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls of ‘1’ made for shrapnel pistols, shrapnel bolters, shrapnel cannon and Gravis shrapnel cannon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3559-5133-8a5e-71e7" name="Apothecarion Detachment (LH)" publicationId="a716-c1c4-7b26-8424" page="116" hidden="false">
      <description>An Apothecarion Detachment is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed to the battlefield, all models in an Apothecarion Detachment must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment of the army they were selected as part of. Legion Apothecaries that have not selected a Legion Spatha combat bike or Legion Scimitar jetbike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type and the same Legiones Hereticus (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary, and may not join units that have Terminator armour of any kind. Legion Apothecaries that have selected a Legion Spatha combat bike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with Legion Spatha combat bikes and the same Legiones Hereticus (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary, and any Legion Apothecaries that have selected a Legion Scimitar jetbike may only be assigned to units composed entirely of models with Legion Scimitar jetbikes and the same Legiones Hereticus (X) special rule as the Legion Apothecary. No Apothecary may be assigned to any unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes an Apothecary as normal during either deployment or any following turn). No more than one Apothecary may be assigned to any given unit.

Once assigned to a unit, the Legion Apothecary is considered part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances – if that unit is removed as a casualty when the Legion Apothecary is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points are ever scored for removing an Legion Apothecary as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Legion Apothecary gains all of the special rules (with the exception of those that specifically forbid it, such as the Bitter Duty special rule) and Unit Sub-types listed for the unit to which it is attached, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to the unit to which it is assigned.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Shattered (LEGION NUMERAL)" id="8fe2-5380-f8a2-1151" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="195+197">
      <description>You can include this model in a Shattered Legions Detachment that includes models representing the version of the Legion Astartes Keyword this model has. When you do so, replace this model’s Legiones Astartes (X) special rule with the Legiones Astartes (Shattered Legions) special rule. This is an exception to the normal rules for Legiones Astartes (Shattered Legions).
When included in a Shattered Legions Detachment, this model must represent the Legion originally present.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lethal Exposure" hidden="false" id="5ec4-39ed-2360-824c" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4">
      <description>If a unit makes attacks with one or more weapons with this special rule as part of a Shooting attack in any Phase, including as part of a Reaction, roll a D6. If the result is equal to or less than the number of weapons in the unit with the Lethal Exposure special rule, the unit suffers a single Wound with no Saves or Damage Mitigation rolls allowed - this wound is allocated to any model in the unit by the controlling player.</description>
    </rule>
<rule id="3917-f2a2-5a53-b4ae" name="Saturnine Terminator Armour" publicationId="ecd9-109b-245d-4083" hidden="false">
<description>A model in Saturnine Terminator armour has a 2+ Armour Save and a 4+ Invulnerable Save, and adds 1 to its Toughness (already included in its profile). It gains the Heavy sub-type and the Bulky (3), Firing Protocols (2) and Slow and Purposeful special rules, and is immune to the Concussive special rule.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8d73-34de-1eac-b67d" name="Spearhead of Saturn" publicationId="ecd9-109b-245d-4083" hidden="false">
<description>The Praetor and any Saturnine Terminator Squad he has joined gain Deep Strike.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="261a-aaba-ab5f-13a7" name="Thermal Diffraction Field" publicationId="ecd9-109b-245d-4083" hidden="false">
<description>Weapons with the Las, Plasma, Melta or Flame traits subtract 1 from their Strength when targeting the Saturnine Dreadnought. In addition, when the Dreadnought rolls for Gets Hot, it may re-roll the result.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6bd6-620e-c9db-b8e5" name="Legends" publicationId="ecd9-109b-245d-4083" hidden="false">
<description>This unit is a Legends unit: a homebrew conversion of a Horus Heresy 3.0 unit (the Age of Darkness: Saturnine box), with playtest profiles and points. Use it only with your opponent&apos;s agreement.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7b74-beea-fbd2-2ae8" name="Relic (X)" publicationId="ecd9-109b-245d-4083" hidden="false">
<description>Ancient artifacts of irreplaceable cultural significance, standard-bearing icons of legendary crusades, or individual warriors carrying the heavy burden of a Legion&apos;s legacy—the loss of such prizes is a catastrophic blow to morale and a major triumph for the foe. If a unit with this Special Rule is destroyed by any means, the opposing player immediately scores a number of additional Victory Points equal to the value of X specified in brackets (e.g., Relic (2) scores 2 additional Victory Points). These Victory Points are awarded in addition to any Victory Points normally scored for destroying the unit (such as those gained from the Price of Failure, Slay the Warlord, or standard Mission-specific objectives). If multiple units with this Special Rule are destroyed during a single battle, the opposing player scores the additional Victory Points for each unit individually.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="32c8-d736-f4a1-7757" name="Expendable (X)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>When a unit with this rule is destroyed, the opposing player scores X fewer Victory Points for it, to a minimum of 0†.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6f7b-1787-b30e-f4bf" name="Inductii" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>A unit that includes any models with this rule may not be selected to fill a compulsory Force Organisation slot, and may not be chosen as the Retinue Squad of any character†.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="0ed0-7c83-2ff1-d694" name="Treacherous Lure (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>a unit made up only of models with this rule may not be targeted by Shooting Attacks in the first game turn. This does not affect Shooting Attacks made as Reactions.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="c1cb-f34d-7471-aaf6" name="Eaters of the Dead (The Thirst)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>after a combat that the unit wins, every enemy unit not in that combat with any model within 8&quot; of it must take a Morale check; if it fails, it Falls Back. This is resolved after everything else from that combat.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="1130-2a9e-dde9-eb84" name="Barbaran Resilience (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>the unit never takes Morale checks for losing 25% or more of its models to Shooting Attacks.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="374d-969d-7719-04ca" name="Perfection Embodied (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>when the unit takes a Morale check or Pinning test in the Shooting phase, roll 3D6 and discard the highest. When it takes a Morale check in the Assault phase, roll 3D6 and discard the lowest.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f1ea-8cc7-1024-8f72" name="Supporting Fire (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>in a turn in which the unit did not move in the Movement phase, its Shooting Attacks gain Pinning.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5554-1df7-6cef-1949" name="Forbidden Augmentations (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>once per battle, when a unit made up only of models with this rule is selected as the target of a Shooting Attack, it gains Feel No Pain (4+) against that attack. Once the attack is resolved, the unit must take a Morale check; if it fails, it becomes Pinned instead of Falling Back. This is a Damage Mitigation roll, and stands in for the 3rd edition Medic! reaction.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="eddb-7370-14d8-a2a7" name="Implacable Advance" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>the unit may fire Rapid Fire weapons at full range after moving, and is never slowed by Difficult Terrain.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="a97b-8442-56fc-cc74" name="Unscrupulous Murderers (The Art of Murder)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>at the end of an Assault phase in which the unit won or drew its combat, roll a D6 for each model in the unit with this rule. For each 6, allocate one Wound (AP –) to any enemy model of your choice locked in that combat; these Wounds are resolved immediately.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="0bf3-909b-9368-4a2d" name="Unchained Conviction (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>whenever a unit made up only of models with this rule would become Pinned, it instead immediately makes a Fall Back move, then automatically Regroups and is not Pinned.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5d75-0f5c-b2da-c31a" name="Wargear of Heroes (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>when resolving a combat, if any models with this rule inflicted at least one unsaved Wound in it that turn, your side scores 1 additional point of combat resolution.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="c3f8-3fbc-5728-a667" name="Creed of Brutality (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>at the start of your turn, the unit may take a Leadership test. If any of its models is within 6&quot; of a friendly Sons of Horus model with WS5 or more, it may use that model&apos;s Leadership. If the test passes, the unit gains Hammer of Wrath (1) until the end of the turn. If it fails, the unit becomes Pinned.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="3a3d-7dc1-621b-dd46" name="Headstrong (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>a unit made up only of models with this rule may declare a charge in a turn in which it Ran. If that charge fails, the unit becomes Pinned.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="a692-cb8f-6a3b-7009" name="Unattuned Practitioners (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>the unit may not select a Prosperine Arcana. Instead, it knows the Ætheric Guidance psychic power. In addition, the unit suffers Perils of the Warp on any double rolled for a Psychic check.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="a621-af11-7bbd-c53e" name="Certainty and Resolve" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>if a unit made up only of models with this rule would Fall Back off a table edge in its own deployment zone, it instead stops at that edge and automatically Regroups. In addition, it rolls 3D6 and discards the highest for Regroup tests.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d5f3-b2c1-dbb5-6844" name="Proof of Valour (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>enemy models with WS5 always need 4+ to hit a unit entirely made up of models with this rule in close combat.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="1d38-336f-8c95-abfd" name="Empty Vessels (Inductii)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>the unit may never be joined by a model without this rule. The first time in a battle that it destroys an enemy unit, it immediately suffers D3 Wounds at AP 2 with no saves of any kind allowed; after that, every model in it gains the Corrupted sub-type and Feel No Pain (6+) for the rest of the battle.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4a78-2a38-14dc-4c03" name="Heedless" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>the unit may never make Reactions other than Advance Reactions.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="3c8a-ccf4-a945-e687" name="Ætheric Guidance (Psychic Power)" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>Used at the start of the unit&apos;s Shooting Attack, by a unit made up only of models with Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons). Take a Psychic check using the unit&apos;s Leadership; if it passes, all of the unit&apos;s ranged weapons (except Blast weapons) gain Breaching (6+) until the end of that Shooting Attack. If it fails, there is no further effect.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="535f-8967-24c5-57df" name="Butcher-Surgeon" publicationId="f7e8-0665-06af-803c" hidden="false">
<description>a Legion Apothecary with Legiones Astartes (World Eaters) who joins this unit gains Ravening Madmen, and once per battle, at the start of your Assault phase, may goad the unit into a frenzy: it gains Furious Charge (1) until the end of the turn. This stands in for the 3rd edition Butcher-Surgeon Prime Advantage†.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="04b8-4f66-af36-9ba9" name="Arch-Sorcerer" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The model has access to all of the Core Psychic Disciplines. When making a Shooting Attack or attacking during an assault, it may use any one Psychic Weapon from any Discipline, regardless of which Psychic Powers it has used that turn. In addition, in each turn it may use any one of the Minor Arcana from the Prosperine Arcana special rule, a different one each turn if it wishes, and automatically passes any Psychic check those require.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6a0b-e3d0-0541-238d" name="Armour of the Word" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The model&apos;s 4+ invulnerable save from Daemonform improves to 3+ against Wounds from weapons with the Force or Psychic Focus special rules, and against Wounds from Perils of the Warp.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="c107-ee1e-8c72-c51f" name="Arrival from the Warp (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Before the first turn, if the Daemon Primarch has not joined a unit and has no Retinue Squad, it may be placed into Reserves; its controlling player declares a turn from 2 to 4 for it to arrive. At the start of that turn, it is placed wholly within 6&quot; of a unit of its own Legion with Legiones Hereticus, and not within 1&quot; of any enemy model; if that is not possible, it tries again at the start of the following turn. Until it arrives, every model in its detachment gains the bonus X given on its datasheet.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8860-2222-53ac-892d" name="Aura of Dark Majesty" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule has a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f650-769f-2099-55e9" name="Aura of Decay" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Enemy units within 6&quot; of a model with this rule subtract 1 from their Initiative and Leadership.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d8fa-2fa1-f73c-808a" name="Battering Onslaught" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule that has two or more melee weapons adds 1 to its Attacks characteristic.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="3dc2-e15d-6664-9319" name="Blind Fury" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule automatically passes any Morale check it takes while locked in combat with an enemy Infantry unit, and never Falls Back from such a combat.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="a2a8-aafd-093f-5be6" name="Bloody Rampage" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>While a model with this rule is locked in combat with one or more enemy Infantry units, it adds 2 to its Attacks characteristic.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8d5d-ae25-810d-a430" name="The Butcher&apos;s Nails" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>At the start of each of the controlling player&apos;s turns after the first, the model gains +1 Attack for the rest of the game, to a maximum of 10 Attacks at the start of the controlling player&apos;s fifth turn. If the model is in Reserves at the start of that turn, its Attacks do not increase. In addition, To Hit rolls made in any Assault phase targeting a unit that includes the model always count that unit&apos;s majority Weapon Skill as 3.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7ff0-bcf9-7c8e-f5b2" name="Carrion Haunter" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A unit with this rule has the Scout special rule. When it makes its Scout move, it is treated as a Vehicle, so it may move up to 12&quot;.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8b38-f014-7cee-a6e4" name="Champions of the Host" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>All models in a unit with this rule are deployed at the same time and need not be placed in unit coherency. From then on, each model is treated as a separate unit.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6acf-0bab-d3e1-e765" name="Corrupted (sub-type)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this sub-type is a Legionary whose body has been given over to a bound warp entity. It has the Daemonic special rule, and counts as a Daemon for any rule that targets or affects Daemons.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="1a8f-098b-ea44-e0f8" name="Crazed" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule may make a Return Fire Reaction without spending a point of its army&apos;s Reaction Allotment.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5715-ad55-1b01-3b5c" name="Daemon Engine (sub-type)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A Dreadnought or Vehicle with this sub-type is a war machine with a daemon bound into its hull. It has the Daemonic and Infernal Regeneration special rules, and counts as a Daemon for any rule that targets or affects Daemons.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="91c9-5eef-850e-e51b" name="Daemon Primarch (unit type)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Each Daemon Primarch uses the official 2.0 Daemon Primarch unit type, takes the Lords of War and Primarchs slot (25% limit), and may be included only once per army.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="2ec1-156b-0151-7501" name="Daemonform" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The model has a 2+ Armour Save and a 4+ Invulnerable Save. While it has half its starting Wounds or fewer, it adds +1 to its It Will Not Die rolls. If, at the start of any of its player turns, it has two or fewer Wounds and is not locked in combat, its controlling player may remove it from play as a casualty; the opposing player then achieves no Objectives or Secondary Objectives for removing it.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8eef-24fd-5ae1-5843" name="Daemonic" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The model has a 5+ invulnerable save. Models with a Wounds characteristic suffer Instant Death from Force weapons. Force weapons gain Armourbane against Vehicle units with this rule.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d094-8a78-aaef-ca9f" name="Daemonic Flight (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>At the start of the controlling player&apos;s Movement phase, the model may set its Movement Characteristic to X for the rest of the turn, gaining the bonus to Charge distance, as Fulgrim Transfigured&apos;s Resplendent Wings.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="ee6a-f4ec-c445-e658" name="Daemonkin" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule may join units with the Corrupted sub-type. A unit with this rule also has the Corrupted sub-type.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="3503-a81b-e010-6209" name="Dark Fury" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule that has two or more melee weapons adds 1 to its Attacks characteristic.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="2ce0-3dc8-4ece-d05a" name="Death to the False Emperor" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Only units with the Traitor allegiance may have this rule. A Character with this rule must issue a challenge whenever it is able to. If it refuses a challenge, its unit counts as having inflicted one fewer Wound when working out combat resolution.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="43be-c770-f6d6-3080" name="Devourer of Souls" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>At the end of an Assault phase in which a model with this rule destroyed one or more enemy models, it regains one lost Wound or Hull Point, up to its starting value.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="9f17-45be-8938-f0c5" name="Explodes (Y&quot;, Z)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>When a model with this rule loses its last Wound or Hull Point, it explodes automatically before it is removed: each unit within Y&quot; suffers Z hits at Strength 5, AP –. The values are given on each datasheet.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="bd28-e858-7f74-f91a" name="Extra Attacks (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with a weapon with this rule makes X additional attacks with that weapon&apos;s profile in melee. These additional attacks only benefit from special rules listed in that weapon&apos;s profile.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="61fe-3c41-3c2d-ae69" name="The Eye of the Crimson King" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>When selecting targets for the model&apos;s psychic powers, all models within range are assumed to be in line of sight, except those Embarked on models with the Transport Sub-type or in Buildings.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7cae-8d53-212b-85cd" name="Fleshmetal Guns" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Each time a unit with this rule shoots its fleshmetal guns, roll three D3 one after the other. The first result is added to 6 to give the weapon&apos;s Strength. The second result is its AP. The third gives the weapon&apos;s special rules: 1 = Murderous Strike (4+); 2 = Exo-shock (4+); 3 = Concussive (1), Pinning and Shell Shock (1). The results apply to every fleshmetal gun in the unit for that Shooting Attack.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f1ea-81a3-1726-0d6b" name="Fleshmetal Weapons" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Each time a unit with this rule fights, roll three D3 one after the other. The first result is added to the models&apos; Strength. The second result is the AP. The third gives the weapon&apos;s special rules: 1 = Murderous Strike (4+); 2 = Exo-shock (4+); 3 = Fleshbane and Precision Strikes (4+). The results apply to every model in the unit for that fight.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5cb7-412e-6c95-89f2" name="The Fortress of the Word" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The model has the Anathemata and Diabolism Psychic Disciplines, and may not select any other.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="bd91-df1d-7811-78ec" name="Frenzied Charge" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>When a model with this rule charges, roll 3D6 and add the results together to determine its charge distance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7fb9-9c71-dc00-8962" name="Gift of the Hellforge" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Friendly Vehicle and Dreadnought units within 6&quot; of one or more models with this rule add 1 to the Attacks and Leadership characteristics of their models, where those models have them. Hellforged units benefit from this rule as normal.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7039-e577-6b05-5053" name="Hateful Assault" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The unit gains Counter-Attack (1). If it already has Counter-Attack, its value increases by 1.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="546c-cdbc-4056-3268" name="Hellfire Reactor" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule has a 5+ invulnerable save against Shooting Attacks and a 4+ invulnerable save against melee attacks.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4fee-d186-0dd1-bcfe" name="Hellforged (sub-type)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A Dreadnought with this sub-type has been rebuilt around a bound daemon. It is not a Daemon Engine. Battlesmith rolls made to repair it are worsened by 1: Battlesmith (4+) becomes 5+, Battlesmith (5+) becomes 6+, and Battlesmith (6+) has no effect on it.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7d46-ace2-dcb7-56ed" name="Herald of the Pantheon" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>An army that includes a model with this rule may fill any non-compulsory slots in its Force Organisation chart with units from the Ruinstorm Daemon army list. These are paid for in points and occupy slots as normal, but must begin the battle in Reserve and may only enter play by means of the Breach the Veil psychic power, as the official Lorgar Transfigured upgrade.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d80e-755a-8346-72e7" name="Horned Raiment" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>If the model is struck by a weapon with the Destroyer type, the number of Wounds it inflicts is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 1.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d332-90eb-15ac-b34b" name="Infernal Augmetics" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule gains It Will Not Die (5+).</description>
</rule>
<rule id="dbea-0f0c-ec74-a57f" name="Infernal Regeneration" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with a Wounds characteristic gains It Will Not Die (5+). A model with Hull Points instead rolls a D6 at the start of each of its controlling player&apos;s turns; on a 5+ it regains one lost Hull Point, up to its starting value.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4173-ff1a-014c-2585" name="Lightning Blows (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>After making To Hit rolls with a weapon with this rule, count the hits scored on rolls of X or more. Immediately make that many additional To Hit rolls against the same unit, using the attacking model&apos;s Weapon Skill. Hits from these rolls wound as normal using this weapon&apos;s profile, or a weapon of the model&apos;s choice if the rule is not on a specific weapon. The additional attacks cannot trigger Lightning Blows again, but benefit from the model&apos;s other special rules, such as Preferred Enemy (X) or Precision Strikes (X).</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5a68-6714-24ff-3788" name="Locus of Power" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Friendly units with the Corrupted sub-type or the Daemonic special rule add 1 to their Strength while they are within 6&quot; of one or more models with this rule.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f8dd-16c7-1f22-afe3" name="Machina Malifica (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>At the end of each Assault phase, roll a D6 for each model with this rule that has lost Wounds. On a roll of X or more, it regains one lost Wound. The value of X is given on each datasheet.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="5d0b-30b5-7f11-f849" name="Master of Mechanisms" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model with this rule has Battlesmith (4+). Instead of using Battlesmith in a turn, it may curse one enemy Vehicle or Dreadnought within 18&quot;: roll a D6, and on a 4+ a Dreadnought suffers one wound, or a Vehicle suffers one glancing hit. No model can be repaired or cursed by more than one model with this rule in the same turn.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="9e8a-ae60-c656-aa97" name="The Power of the Word" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Any Legion Command Squad, Cataphractii Command Squad or Tartaros Command Squad selected as a Retinue Squad with the model as its leader gains Fearless and Feel No Pain (4+). In addition, once per battle, one friendly unit composed entirely of Infantry or Cavalry with at least one model within 18&quot; of the model (but not a unit that includes it) may be selected at the start of any Game Turn; it gains Fearless and Feel No Pain (4+) for that Game Turn.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="93d6-1709-1467-e9a8" name="Preternatural Resilience" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Any hits allocated to the model with Poisoned (X), Rending (X) or Fleshbane only affect it on a D6 roll of 6, instead of their usual effect. While the model has joined a unit, this special rule has no effect.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="382e-57df-49c9-1614" name="Red Sands" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>In any turn the model may make as many Challenges as there are enemy Characters or Primarchs locked in combat with it, up to its current Attacks. It fights them in an order of its controlling player&apos;s choosing, but any enemy Primarch must be fought first, and it must divide its Attacks between them, devoting at least one to each Challenge.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6c32-ded7-ef22-2a03" name="Reservoir of Daemonic Energy" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A friendly Master of Possession within 6&quot; of one or more models with this rule adds 1 to its Leadership when taking Psychic checks.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="71cb-ec4e-1ba8-cab7" name="Rite of Possession" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Enemy Psykers within 12&quot; of one or more models with this rule suffer Perils of the Warp on any double rolled for a Psychic check.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f87b-c3d3-ace6-5241" name="Runes of the Blood God" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>An enemy Psyker that targets a model with this rule with a psychic power suffers Perils of the Warp on any double rolled for that Psychic check. A model with this rule cannot be targeted by psychic powers manifested by friendly Psykers.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="e479-505d-4744-c39a" name="Scion of Corruption (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Every unit with the Legiones Astartes (X) special rule in the same army must replace it with Legiones Hereticus (X). A Daemon Primarch cannot be included in the same army as the Primarch it is based on.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7d79-c802-c765-41b9" name="Scuttling Gait" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>When a model with this rule Runs, it adds 6&quot; to its Movement instead of its normal Run distance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7ce4-acf4-4299-7334" name="Shadow of the Reaper" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>So long as the model is not embarked, in Reserves, locked in combat or part of a unit with the Retinue or Deathshroud Retinue special rules, in its Shooting phase, instead of making a Shooting Attack, it may be removed and redeployed anywhere within 10&quot; of its original position, not within 3&quot; of an enemy model or in Impassable Terrain, a Vehicle or a Building. This counts as an alternative form of movement and ignores intervening terrain. It may Charge normally that turn, but counts as making a Disordered Charge.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="eee8-e11b-15e1-792a" name="Teleport Strike" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The unit has the Deep Strike special rule.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="6e11-32d3-35e2-862f" name="Writhing Tentacles" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>When a unit with this rule is selected to fight, roll a D3. The result is the Attacks characteristic of each model in the unit for that fight.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4e41-306d-2e9b-e883" name="Wrathful Blows (X)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>A model making Attacks with a weapon with this special rule makes an amount of Attacks equal to the number shown in brackets, regardless of their Attacks Characteristic and any bonuses gained for Charging.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d0a9-3362-1995-9f39" name="Legiones Hereticus (Alpha Legion)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Alpha Legion)&apos;.

• Lies Within Lies: after both armies have deployed, the controlling player may remove one unit with this rule and redeploy it anywhere in their deployment zone, or place it in Reserves.
• Veiled by the Warp: against Shooting Attacks from more than 12&quot; away, the unit has Shrouded (6+), or improves an existing Shrouded by 1.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="7417-5bb1-54d7-d9ea" name="Legiones Hereticus (Death Guard)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Death Guard) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Death Guard)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Death Guard)&apos;.

• Inexorable: the unit may move and fire Heavy weapons as though it had not moved, but may never Run or Advance.
• Plague-ridden: the unit has Feel No Pain (6+), or improves an existing Feel No Pain by 1; this is a Damage Mitigation roll.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="caf2-c1d5-1bf7-3be6" name="Legiones Hereticus (Night Lords)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Night Lords) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Night Lords)&apos;.

• Midnight Terror: enemy units within 12&quot; of one or more units with this rule subtract 1 from their Leadership.
• Prey on the Weak: models with this rule add 1 to their To Hit rolls in melee against units that are Pinned, Falling Back or below half their starting number of models.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="157a-806d-be7f-4a4d" name="Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Sons of Horus)&apos;.

• Death Dealers: pistols and bolt weapons used by models with this rule gain Rending (6+) when firing at targets within 12&quot;.
• Merciless Fighters: while locked in combat with an enemy unit that has fewer models than the unit with this rule, each model with this rule adds 1 to its Attacks.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4922-cbab-aff6-3056" name="Legiones Hereticus (Thousand Sons)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Thousand Sons)&apos;.

• Cult of Change: every model with the Infantry or Cavalry Unit Type gains the Psyker Sub-type. Characters with this rule may select one Minor Arcana as the Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) rule allows; this is an exception to the loss of Legion options.
• Sorcerous Hubris: a unit with this rule may re-roll a failed Psychic check once per phase, but if the re-roll also fails, Perils of the Warp inflicts one additional Wound.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="2bd3-26ac-6b3a-427b" name="Legiones Hereticus (Word Bearers)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (Word Bearers)&apos;.

• Daemonic Communion: the unit has Adamantium Will (5+), and Feel No Pain (6+) against Wounds caused by Psychic weapons and Perils of the Warp. This is a Damage Mitigation roll.
• Unholy Fervour: a model with this rule may never have its Leadership modified below 7. If a combat involving one or more models with this rule ends in a draw, their side counts as winning by 1.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="790f-d203-4078-2019" name="Legiones Hereticus (World Eaters)" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>This special rule completely replaces the Legiones Astartes (World Eaters) special rule. A unit with it loses access to that Legion&apos;s unique wargear, Consul upgrades, Rites of War and Advanced Reaction, unless the Legiones Hereticus conversion says otherwise. A Warlord with it may select the Warlord Traits of its Legion, replacing each instance of &apos;Legiones Astartes (World Eaters)&apos; in that trait with &apos;Legiones Hereticus (World Eaters)&apos;.

• Heedless: the unit may never make a Fall Back move voluntarily, and may not make Return Fire or Overwatch reactions.
• Skulls for the Skull Throne: on any turn in which a unit with this rule makes a successful Charge, it gains +1 Attack for the remainder of that turn, even if the Charge is a Disordered Charge. In addition, in any Assault phase in which the unit destroys an enemy unit, every model in it regains one lost Wound, up to its starting value.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f3c2-7bd2-89c5-3b69" name="Daemon Powers: Gifts of the Blood God" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Khorne despises sorcery, and his favoured son has no use for it. Angron&apos;s gifts are rage, slaughter and the skulls of champions. These are not psychic powers and need no Psychic check.

• The Red Angel&apos;s Wrath (Nuceria): once per battle, in a turn in which Angron charged, after the charge is resolved, every enemy unit locked in combat with him suffers D6 hits at Strength 7, AP 3, as the rage that ascended him on Nuceria bursts outward.
• Contempt for the Witch: Angron has Adamantium Will (2+), and enemy Psykers within 12&quot; of him suffer Perils of the Warp on any double rolled for a Psychic check.
• Skulls for the Throne: each time Angron removes an enemy Character or Primarch as a casualty in a Challenge, he immediately regains D3 lost Wounds, up to his starting value.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="c7a2-6b2d-f83e-cfb8" name="Daemon Powers: Gifts of the Pantheon" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Lorgar raised the Word Bearers&apos; cathedrals to all four Powers and was the first to kneel. As a Daemon Primarch he speaks with the voice of the Pantheon itself. These are not psychic powers and need no Psychic check.

• Litanies of the Primordial Truth (Colchis): The Power of the Word may be used twice per battle instead of once, and its range increases to 24&quot;.
• The Shadow Crusade: once per battle, at the start of your turn, one Ruinstorm Daemon unit in Reserve may enter play within 12&quot; of Lorgar without needing Breach the Veil, as the Word Bearers did when they tore open the Ruinstorm across Ultramar.
• Golden Visage of the Urizen: Lorgar has Fear (2), and enemy units within 12&quot; of him subtract 1 from their Leadership.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d28f-4970-48d9-4ff2" name="Daemon Powers: Gifts of the Changer of Ways" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>Magnus bargained his Legion&apos;s flesh to Tzeentch to warn his father of Horus, and paid for it at Prospero. As a Daemon Primarch he wields the Warp without limit. These are psychic powers, used in addition to those Arch-Sorcerer allows, and need a Psychic check as normal.

• The Burning of Prospero (Psychic Weapon): see the Armoury. Magnus may use this psychic weapon in addition to the one Arch-Sorcerer allows.
• Time Flux: in your Movement phase, friendly Thousand Sons units within 12&quot; of Magnus add 2&quot; to their Movement and charge distances until the end of the turn.
• The Great Eye&apos;s Gaze: once per turn, Magnus may re-roll any one dice roll made for himself or a friendly unit within 12&quot;, as he sees every thread of fate.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="4777-79e4-b61d-54e5" name="Daemon Powers: Gifts of the Plague God" publicationId="0b44-e890-1d51-5b89" hidden="false">
<description>The Primarch who loathed psykers above all things became one. Lost in the Warp with his Legion dying of the Destroyer Plague, Mortarion begged for deliverance and Nurgle answered, filling him with the Grandfather&apos;s sorcery. He wields it with the same bitter, grudging discipline he once turned against the witches of Barbarus. Mortarion is a Psyker; the powers below marked as psychic need a Psychic check as normal, and he may use one psychic power and one psychic weapon each turn.

• Rotwind (Psychic Weapon): see the Armoury. A howling gale of pestilence, the Destroyer Plague given form. He may fire it instead of, or as well as, the Lantern.
• Miasma of Pestilence (Psychic Power, Shooting phase): choose Mortarion&apos;s unit or one friendly Death Guard unit within 12&quot;; until the start of your next turn, it is wreathed in a cloud of flies and filth and has Shrouded (5+).
• Blades of Putrefaction (Psychic Power, Assault phase): choose Mortarion&apos;s unit or one friendly Death Guard unit within 12&quot;; until the end of the phase, its melee weapons gain Poisoned (4+), and its Melee attacks that already have Poisoned (X) improve it by 1, to a best of 2+.
• Putrescent Vitality (Psychic Power, Movement phase): choose one friendly Death Guard unit within 12&quot; (not Mortarion); until the start of your next turn, its models add +1 to their Strength and Toughness.
• Nurgle&apos;s Rot (not psychic): at the start of each of your turns, every enemy unit within 6&quot; of Mortarion suffers one hit at Strength 4, AP –, with Poisoned (4+).
• The Reaper Walks (not psychic): Shadow of the Reaper may redeploy Mortarion up to 14&quot; instead of 10&quot;, and he does not count as making a Disordered Charge in a turn he uses it.</description>
</rule>
  </sharedRules>
